## 6. Data Principal Rights

Under the DPDP Act 2023, you have the right to:

1. **Access** your personal data held by us (Section 11).
2. **Correction** of inaccurate or outdated personal data (Section 12).
3. **Erasure** of personal data where processing is no longer necessary (Section 12).
4. **Grievance Redressal** through our Data Protection Officer (Section 13).
5. **Nominate** another person to exercise rights on your behalf (Section 14).

To exercise any of these rights, contact **{{dpoEmail}}** with the subject line "Data Principal Rights Request — {{organizationName}}".

